# Regenerable run artifacts. What IS tracked: report.md, compare.py, injector.py,
# write_inlet_field.py, and of_case/{system,run_of.sh} -- the case TEMPLATE.
#
# The whole scratch case is regenerated by of_case/run_of.sh, which copies the mesh, the physical
# properties and the frozen flow from ../bfs3d_openfoam/of_case rather than storing a second copy:
# this case has no mesh and no flow of its own, and duplicating them would let the two drift.
#
# No trailing slash on `runs`: in a git worktree it is often a symlink to a shared run directory,
# and git treats a symlink as a file, so a `runs/` rule would not match it and it would get staged.
runs
*.log
of_case/constant/
of_case/[0-9]*/
of_case/log.*
of_case/postProcessing/
of_case/processor*/
__pycache__/
*.npz
# The tracer's inlet field is GENERATED from injector.injected_value by write_inlet_field.py, on the
# mesh it will be read against. Committing it would put a second, silently-drifting copy of the
# injection profile in the repository -- the exact duplication the generator exists to prevent.
of_case/0.orig/s
